 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "File storage in Azure Blob Storage, so images and documents live in the cloud rather than on a disk.",
  "forArchitect": "The Assets adapter for clustered deployments: shared storage is what lets several instances serve the same files. One dependency, no schema, configuration only.",
  "forDeveloper": "Go through the blob abstraction, not the Azure SDK, or your module stops working on the file-system provider. CDN in front of the container is the usual pairing.",
  "owns": [],
